---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy | HealthChrono"
  description="Learn how HealthChrono protects and encrypts your personal health data with zero-knowledge local storage, AES-256 encryption, and GDPR/CCPA compliance."
>
  <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-16 border-b border-slate-800">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-900/60 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/30 mb-4">
        Privacy & Trust
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight font-heading">HealthChrono Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-400 text-sm">
        <strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 25, 2026 &bull; Effective Date: September 25, 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        
        <section class="bg-emerald-50/60 border border-emerald-200 rounded-2xl p-6 text-sm">
          <h2 class="text-emerald-900 font-bold text-base mb-2 font-heading">Our Privacy Pledge: No Ad Trackers, No Data Brokers</h2>
          <p class="text-emerald-800">
            HealthChrono was built under the premise that health records belong solely to the individual. We do not sell your personal health data to third-party data brokers, insurers, or advertising networks. Your records are stored locally with AES-256 hardware encryption.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            Welcome to <strong>HealthChrono</strong> ("we," "our," or "us"). We are dedicated to maintaining the highest confidentiality, integrity, and security standards for your personal health records. This Privacy Policy explains how our mobile application and accompanying web portal collect, use, encrypt, store, and protect your information when you use our service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">2. Information We Collect</h2>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-4 mb-2">2.1 Self-Reported Health Information</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Symptom logs:</strong> Self-reported physical or mental symptoms, date/time stamps, severity levels rated on a 1–10 scale, and trigger notes.</li>
            <li><strong>Medication regimens:</strong> Prescription drug names, dosage amounts, scheduled timing, dose frequency, and self-recorded dose adherence markers.</li>
            <li><strong>Physician reports:</strong> Custom date ranges and generated clinical PDF summaries formatted for discussion with your healthcare providers.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-4 mb-2">2.2 Account & Authentication Data</h3>
          <p>
            If you create a synced cloud account, we collect your email address and authentication tokens via our secure authentication provider (Clerk). If you choose to use HealthChrono in offline-only mode, no personal identifying account credentials are transmitted to any server.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-4 mb-2">2.3 Device & Diagnostics (Anonymized)</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Technical device details:</strong> Device model, operating system version (iOS/Android), and application build version.</li>
            <li><strong>Crash & performance reports:</strong> Anonymized diagnostic logs stripped of personally identifiable information (PII) to resolve bugs and runtime crashes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p>We process your data strictly for legitimate operational purposes:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li>To operate and maintain local symptom tracking and medication management.</li>
            <li>To deliver local push notifications and alarms for medication doses.</li>
            <li>To compile and export structured clinical PDF reports upon your explicit command.</li>
            <li>To synchronize encrypted records between your authorized mobile devices if cloud backup is enabled.</li>
            <li>To maintain application reliability and provide customer support when requested.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">4. Cryptographic Security & Local Storage</h2>
          <p>We implement defense-in-depth security architecture:</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-4">
            <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1 text-sm">Hardware-Backed Local Encryption</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
                All records stored on your device are encrypted at rest with AES-256 utilizing platform-managed hardware keystores (iOS Keychain and Android KeyStore).
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-50">
              <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1 text-sm">Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3)</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
                All network transmissions between your device and our cloud backend are encrypted in transit using TLS 1.3 cryptographic protocols with modern cipher suites.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            You can also configure the in-app <strong>Biometric Lock</strong> (Face ID, Touch ID, or biometric device lock) to prevent unauthorized local physical access to the application.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">5. Data Retention Policy</h2>
          <p>We retain data only as long as necessary to fulfill the services:</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
            <table class="w-full text-left border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden text-sm">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-900 font-semibold border-b border-slate-200">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3">Category</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Retention Duration</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 text-xs">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Active Health Logs</td>
                  <td class="p-3">While account is active</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Retained on-device until manually deleted by the user.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Cloud Sync Backups</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Duration of account / 30-day purge</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Encrypted backups purged within 30 days of account deletion.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Inactive Accounts</td>
                  <td class="p-3">2 years from last activity</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Accounts dormant over 24 months are flagged for automated deletion.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Diagnostic Logs</td>
                  <td class="p-3">90 days</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Stripped error telemetry and stack traces.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">6. Account & Data Deletion</h2>
          <p>
            You have absolute control over your health data. You may delete your account and all associated health records at any time:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>In-App Self-Service:</strong> Open the app, navigate to <strong>Settings &gt; Data Management &gt; Delete Account</strong>, and confirm. All records stored on your device and synchronized in the cloud will be permanently and irreversibly destroyed.</li>
            <li><strong>Web Deletion Portal:</strong> Visit our dedicated <a href="/delete-data" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold underline">Account & Data Deletion Request Page</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Email Support:</strong> Send a deletion request to <a href="mailto:info@drit.ninja" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold underline">info@drit.ninja</a>. We process verified deletion requests within 3 business days.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">7. Data Breach Notification</h2>
          <p>
            In compliance with the FTC Health Breach Notification Rule and state privacy statutes, in the unlikely event of an unauthorized acquisition or breach affecting your personal health information, HealthChrono will notify affected individuals and regulatory authorities within 60 calendar days of breach confirmation, outlining the incident details, affected data fields, and mitigation recommendations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">8. Your Privacy Rights (GDPR & CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
          <p>
            Under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the California Consumer Privacy Act / California Privacy Rights Act (CCPA/CPRA), and related privacy laws, you possess the right to:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request confirmation of what personal data we process and inspect copies of your records.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Portability:</strong> Export your complete health log history in structured, machine-readable formats (PDF, CSV, JSON) directly through app settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> Correct any inaccurate or incomplete records directly within the app interface.</li>
            <li><strong>Erasure (Right to be Forgotten):</strong> Request the permanent deletion of your account and cloud records.</li>
            <li><strong>Opt-Out of Data Sales:</strong> HealthChrono does not sell or share personal health information for behavioral advertising or monetary consideration.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">9. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
          <p>
            We engage vetted third-party infrastructure providers under strict Data Processing Agreements:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Clerk:</strong> Secure user authentication and token issuance.</li>
            <li><strong>Supabase:</strong> High-security cloud database hosting encrypted sync records.</li>
            <li><strong>RevenueCat:</strong> In-App Purchase and subscription status management (Apple App Store / Google Play).</li>
            <li><strong>Sentry:</strong> Anonymized, non-PII error and crash reporting for software stability.</li>
            <li><strong>Netlify:</strong> Static web hosting and secure SSL delivery for this website.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">10. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA)</h2>
          <p>
            HealthChrono is intended for users who are at least 13 years of age (or 16 in the European Economic Area). We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal health data, please contact us immediately at <a href="mailto:info@drit.ninja" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold underline">info@drit.ninja</a> and we will delete the data promptly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-heading mb-3">11. Contact Us & Privacy Officer</h2>
          <p>
            For any privacy inquiries, data subject access requests, or regulatory communications:
          </p>
          <div class="mt-4 p-5 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl space-y-1 text-sm">
            <p><strong>HealthChrono Inc.</strong></p>
            <p>Attn: Privacy & Data Protection Officer</p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:info@drit.ninja" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold underline">info@drit.ninja</a></p>
            <p>Website: <a href="https://gethealthchrono.com" class="text-emerald-600 font-semibold underline">https://gethealthchrono.com</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
